{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1465933-running-farscape-or-similar-style-game-and-the-path-system","id":1465933,"title":"Running Farscape, or similar style game, and the path system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-30T11:45:05-07:00","id":1465933,"title":"Running Farscape, or similar style game, and the path system","content":"Okay, say I want to play astronaut John Crichton, a brilliant scientist and member of IASA, an international space agency devoted to exploration that was founded by Talents from all the world nations space agencies who banded together to better explore the unknown. A major part of the games story is that my character is going to be shot through a wormhole to a distant part of the Galaxy. Now, my character does have a defined Allegiance that is important to his character, but no access to connections, contacts or resources available to him because of that Allegiance. What would be a good way to deal with this situation in the game system? Maybe keep the characters paths and let them develop new, appropriate contacts and connections? Give the a new, &quot;Lost Astronaut&quot; path to replace the IASA Allegiance, and just have the IASA connection by background? Also what about other paths that you don't have access to because you are far away? You can't really talk to your college professor if you are halfway across the Galaxy. Have the character form a new, similar connection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T00:24:03-07:00","id":1465980,"title":"","